It starts at 2:07 a.m.

Micro Nick wakes everyone up by repeatedly hitting a spoon against a coffee mug.

tink.

tink.

tink.

Jessica:

“I swear to God, if this is another timeline—”

Micro Nick:

“Richmond.”

Regular Cage bolts upright.

“Virginia?”

Little Nick:

“No, Richmond, Luxembourg. YES, VIRGINIA.”

Micro Nick rolls out a map.

There are two red circles.

One at VMI.

One over Monument Avenue.

Jessica looks at it.

“No.”

Cage hasn’t said anything yet.

“No.”

Cage slowly reaches for his jacket.

“Jessica—”

“NO.”

Little Nick is already putting on a miniature Civil War-era kepi that nobody remembers buying.

Jessica points at him.

“Where did you even get that?”

Little Nick:

“Quartermaster.”

“We don’t HAVE a quartermaster.”

From inside a kitchen cabinet:

“Morning.”

Jessica opens it.

There is a man in camouflage eating Cheerios.

She closes it again.

“We’re moving.”

