Apparently, according to Micro Nick, the universe has suffered a historical continuity inversion.

Not history changing.

Much stupider.

Certain historical objects have become convinced they’re supposed to be somewhere else.

Stone statues, specifically.

Cage listens gravely.

“So they’re homesick.”

Jessica:

“They are rocks.”

Cage:

“That is an unnecessarily reductive interpretation of masonry.”

And according to Micro Nick, one particular statue needs to return to VMI before sunrise, while several old Monument Avenue pedestals have begun emitting what Unit 4 technically classifies as:

“Confederate Santa energy.”

Jessica:

“What the fuck is Confederate Santa energy?”

Marjorie from Unit 4 turns her laptop around.

Security footage.

At exactly midnight, a bronze horse appears on an empty pedestal.

At 12:04, another statue manifests two blocks away.

At 12:09, somebody’s Ring camera records an eleven-foot Nicolas Cage dragging a cannon down the sidewalk.

Everyone slowly turns toward Big Nick.

Big Nick:

“THAT WASN’T ME.”

Little Nick:

“That is exactly what someone who dragged a cannon would say.”

Big Nick:

“I WOULD HAVE CARRIED IT.”

Reasonable point.

