And that is how, according to Unit 4’s sealed incident report, Nicolas Cage spent one October night flying back and forth across Virginia in a scooter-powered sleigh, delivering historically misplaced statuary like the world’s most constitutionally confusing Santa Claus.

At every stop:

THOOM.

Big Nick lands.

Regular Cage checks the map.

Little Nick checks the manifest.

Micro Nick checks reality.

Jessica sits in the passenger seat questioning every decision that led to her being here.

And Cage climbs down a chimney despite the fact that the statue very obviously will not fit.

Jessica:

“NICOLAS. USE THE FRONT DOOR.”

Muffled from chimney:

“THAT’S NOT HOW CHRISTMAS WORKS.”

Big Nick, standing on the roof with a seven-hundred-pound bronze horse:

